---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets"
import CaseStudy from "@/layouts/case-study.astro"
import { getProject } from "@/data/projects"
import envelopeImg from "@/assets/projects/ncga-stationery/envelope-editor.png"

const project = getProject("ncga-stationery-templates")!

const pictureFormats: ("avif" | "webp")[] = ["avif", "webp"]
const pictureWidths = [640, 960, 1280]
const pictureSizes = "(min-width: 768px) 960px, 100vw"
---

<CaseStudy
  project={project}
  title="NCGA Stationery Template System"
  seoTitle="NCGA Stationery Template System · Information Architecture"
  seoDescription="Designing a constrained template engine for NCGA legislator letterhead and envelopes: LOCKED vs DATA-DRIVEN fields, print-accurate preview, and fewer production mistakes."
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The North Carolina General Assembly print shop produces repeat stationery
    for all 170 legislators. Same formal brand requirements every time,
    different contact data, committee lists, and chamber wording. Before the
    system, repeat orders relied on separate files per legislator, and small
    differences in spacing, ink color, and committee data compounded across all
    170.
  </p>

  <h2>LOCKED vs DATA-DRIVEN</h2>
  <p>
    Production-approved variation lives in a typed <strong
      >LegislatorRecord</strong
    >; everything else stays out of reach. <strong>LOCKED</strong>: the state
    seal, the “North Carolina General Assembly” masthead, licensed typefaces,
    page grid, margins, recycle mark geometry. <strong>DATA-DRIVEN</strong>:
    member name, chamber, office address, phone, committees, and ink color, with
    visibility toggles that hide sections without deleting the data.
  </p>

  <div class="template-flow" aria-label="Legislator record to output">
    <div class="template-flow__node">
      <span>Input</span>
      <strong>LegislatorRecord</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="template-flow__connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="template-flow__node template-flow__node--wide">
      <span>Locked template</span>
      <strong>Seal, masthead, grid, type</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="template-flow__connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="template-flow__node">
      <span>Output</span>
      <strong>Letterhead or envelope PDF</strong>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Same Record, Different Surfaces</h2>
  <p>
    Letterhead and envelopes share one data model but not one form. The envelope
    editor drops phone and committees, omits the seal to match production
    artwork, and constrains return addresses to two NCGA buildings with fixed
    ZIP codes. Recipient addresses defer to a downstream mail merge.
  </p>

  <figure class="case-figure">
    <Picture
      src={envelopeImg}
      alt="Envelope editor with building picker and print-accurate envelope preview."
      formats={pictureFormats}
      widths={pictureWidths}
      sizes={pictureSizes}
    />
    <figcaption>
      Envelope surface: building picker instead of free-text address, no seal,
      recipients added later by mail merge.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Outcome</h2>
  <p>
    Preview is sized in real inches and points, and PDF output uses a second
    renderer that shares the same logic for chamber copy, ink colors, and
    visible committees. Personalized mailings to all 170 members now go out in
    one press pass instead of two.
  </p>
  <p>
    Related NCGA work not shown here includes a press-split calculator, identity
    work, job tickets, proofing, and high-volume production workflows.
  </p>
</CaseStudy>

<style>
  .template-flow {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
  }

  .template-flow__node {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--background) 96%, var(--muted));
  }

  .template-flow__node span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .template-flow__node strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .template-flow__connector {
    width: 1px;
    height: 1.25rem;
    margin-left: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--border);
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .template-flow {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 2rem minmax(0, 1.2fr) 2rem minmax(
          0,
          1fr
        );
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0;
    }

    .template-flow__connector {
      width: 100%;
      height: 1px;
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
